= Calculus Language Quiz

_5 questions. Choose the best answer for each._

== Question 1

Which of the following is equivalent to $log_2 16$?

a) $log_10 16 / log_10 2$

b) $2 log_2 8$

c) $log_2 8 + log_2 2$

d) All of the above

== Question 2

If $f(x) = x^2 - 3$ and $g(x) = 2x + 1$, what is $(f compose g)(x)$?

a) $2x^2 - 5$

b) $4x^2 + 4x - 2$

c) $(2x + 1)^2 - 3$

d) $2(x^2 - 3) + 1$

== Question 3

The graph of $y = f(x - 2) + 3$ is obtained from $y = f(x)$ by:

a) Shifting left 2 units and up 3 units

b) Shifting right 2 units and up 3 units

c) Shifting left 2 units and down 3 units

d) Shifting right 2 units and down 3 units

== Question 4

Using the half-angle formula, $sin^2(pi/8)$ equals:

a) $(1 - sqrt(2)/2)/2$

b) $(1 - sqrt(2)/2)/4$

c) $(1 + sqrt(2)/2)/2$

d) $sqrt((1 - sqrt(2)/2)/2)$

== Question 5

Which function has a domain of all real numbers except $x = 0$?

a) $f(x) = ln x$

b) $f(x) = 1/x$

c) $f(x) = sqrt(x)$

d) $f(x) = e^x$

